  "threatScenario": "An actor string contains a C0 control character, so the manifest canonicalizes differently depending on whether the implementation escapes it. RFC 8785 requires \\u0007; emitting the raw byte produces different signed bytes and rejects a valid manifest, and a control character in an attribution field is also how a tampered actor can be made to render as a different name in a log or UI.",
